<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Sprint 0 — Project Charter</title><!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><w:WordDocument><w:View>Print</w:View><w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom></w:WordDocument></xml><![endif]--><style>@page{size:21cm 29.7cm;margin:2.5cm 2.2cm;mso-header-margin:1cm;mso-footer-margin:1cm;}body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;}h1{font-size:19pt;color:#0d2b45;border-bottom:3px solid #1f7a8c;padding-bottom:5pt;margin:0 0 6pt;}h2{font-size:14pt;color:#0d2b45;border-bottom:1px solid #9db8cc;padding-bottom:3pt;margin:20pt 0 6pt;page-break-after:avoid;}h3{font-size:12pt;color:#1f7a8c;margin:12pt 0 4pt;page-break-after:avoid;}p{margin:0 0 7pt;text-align:justify;}.es{color:#3d4c5c;font-style:italic;border-left:2pt solid #c0392b;padding-left:8pt;}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:6pt 0 12pt;}td,th{border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;}th{background:#12324a;color:#fff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;text-align:left;}.cover{text-align:center;}.cover .inst{font-size:13pt;font-weight:bold;color:#0d2b45;letter-spacing:1pt;}.cover .big{font-size:24pt;font-weight:bold;color:#12324a;margin:22pt 0 4pt;}.cover .sub{font-size:13pt;color:#1f7a8c;}.pb{page-break-before:always;}.mono{font-family:Consolas,"Courier New",monospace;font-size:9.5pt;}.hint{color:#8a94a0;font-style:italic;font-size:9.5pt;}.box{border:1px solid #9db8cc;background:#f2f7fb;padding:8pt 10pt;margin:8pt 0;}ul,ol{margin:0 0 8pt 18pt;}li{margin-bottom:3pt;}</style></head><body><div class="cover"><p class="inst">INSTITUTO NACIONAL DE EDUCACIÓN LOURDES — INDEL</p><p>Bachillerato Técnico Vocacional en Desarrollo de Software</p><p>Module 3.6 — English for IT Systems</p><p class="big">SPRINT 0<br>PROJECT CHARTER</p><p class="sub">Activity 04 — Build It in English · Day 1</p><p class="es">Acta de arranque del proyecto · Actividad 04 · Día 1</p><br><table style="width:82%;margin:0 auto"><tr><th style="width:38%">Student / Estudiante</th><td>Rodrigo Carballo - Cristian Navas - Jefferson Arce - Anderson Ávila</td></tr><tr><th>Grade and section / Grado y sección</th><td>3° DS "A"</td></tr><tr><th>Project / Proyecto</th><td>Signal Desk</td></tr><tr><th>Environment / Entorno</th><td>C # - MAUI</td></tr><tr><th>IDE and version</th><td>Visual Studio Community 21 - .NET 10</td></tr><tr><th>Date / Fecha</th><td>2026-09-01</td></tr><tr><th>Teacher / Docente</th><td>Ing. Javier Arturo García Mineros</td></tr></table></div><div class="pb"></div><h1>1. Purpose of the application</h1><p>Signal Desk is an application designed to help system operators track and manage operational incidents as they happen. The system provides a single dashboard where users can log new alerts, change their status, and filter events based on priority. Its main goal is to help technical teams respond faster to errors and keep the system running smoothly</p><p class="es">Signal Desk es una aplicación diseñada para ayudar a los operadores del sistema a registrar y dar seguimiento a los incidentes operativos en tiempo real. La herramienta ofrece un panel centralizado donde se pueden reportar alertas, cambiar su estado y filtrarlas según su nivel de urgencia. Su objetivo principal es acelerar el tiempo de respuesta del equipo técnico y mantener la estabilidad del sistema.</p><h1>2. User stories</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">#</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">AS A … I WANT … SO THAT …</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">1</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a system operator, I want to create a new signal record with its severity level so that the team knows about potential errors.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">The system checks that required fields like Title and Priority are filled before saving</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">2</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As an admin, I want to see a main dashboard with all active signals so that I can monitor overall system health.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">The dashboard loads automatically and clearly displays the status of each signal.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">3</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As an operator, I want to filter signals by priority so that I can focus on resolving critical issues first</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">The list updates immediately when applying a filter without freezing the screen</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">4</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As an admin, I want to change a signal's status to "Resolved" so that everyone knows the issue was fixed</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Saving the update changes the status tag and logs the exact time of resolution.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">5</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As an operator, I want to remove old or duplicated signals so that the screen stays organized.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">A confirmation message pops up before deleting any record to prevent mistakes</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">6</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a user, I want to export the signal history so that I can share event logs with managers</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">The application generates a readable summary file containing the recorded signals</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>3. Screens and controls</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">SCREEN OR VIEW</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">CONTROLS (NAMED IN ENGLISH)</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">WHAT THE USER DOES THERE</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">MainDashboardView</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">txtSignalTitle, cmbPriority, txtDescription, btnAddSignal, dgvSignalList</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Logs new operational signals, selects priority levels, and views the active incident list in real time</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">SignalDetailsView</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">lblSignalId, lblTimestamp, cmbStatus, btnUpdateStatus, btnDeleteSignal</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Reviews specific signal details, updates resolution status, or deletes obsolete alerts.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">ReportsView</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">dtpStartDate, dtpEndDate, btnExportData, lblSummaryStats</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Filters signal history by date range and exports logs to a local file</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="pb"></div><h1>4. Data model</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">CLASS</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">FIELDS AND TYPES</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">WHERE THE DATA LIVES (MEMORY / FILE)</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Signal</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">int Id, string Title, string Description, string Priority, string Status, DateTime CreatedAt</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">In-memory List (List&lt;Signal&gt;)</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">SignalReport</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">int TotalSignals, int ResolvedSignals, DateTime ExportDate, string FilePath</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Local File (JSON / TXT)</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">&nbsp;</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>5. Setup log</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">STEP</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">COMMAND OR ACTION</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">RESULT</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">PROBLEM FOUND AND HOW YOU SOLVED IT</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Install / verify SDK</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">dotnet --version</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">SDK version displayed correctly</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">No SDK found initially; downloaded and installed .NET SDK from official website</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Create project</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">dotnet new winforms -o SignalDesk</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Project template generated successfully</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Incorrect project name spelling; deleted folder and re-ran command with correct casing</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">First run</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">dotnet run</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Application compiled and empty form launched</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Build error due to missing dependencies; resolved by running dotnet restore</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Folder structure</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Created /Models, /Views, /Services folders</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Project structure organized cleanly.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">None encountered.</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>6. Risks</h1><p>1. Risk: Unhandled exceptions when saving data could crash the application.<br><br>Mitigation: Implement try-catch blocks and user error messages for all input and file operations.<br><br>2. Risk: Miscommunication on control names across team members.<br><br>Mitigation: Follow the established English naming conventions for controls (btn, txt, cmb, dgv) strictly</p><p class="es">1. Riesgo: Excepciones no controladas al guardar datos que puedan cerrar la aplicación inesperadamente.<br><br>Mitigación: Implementar bloques try-catch y mensajes de error claros para el usuario en todas las operaciones de datos.<br><br>2. Riesgo: Falta de estandarización en los nombres de los controles entre los miembros del equipo.<br><br>Mitigación: Seguir estrictamente las convenciones de nomenclatura en inglés definidas (btn, txt, cmb, dgv).</p><div class="box"><b>Evidence:</b> attach screenshot EV-01 showing the empty project running, and the content of your README.md file.<br><span class="es">Adjunte la captura EV-01 con el proyecto vacío en ejecución y el contenido de su README.md.</span></div><br><br><table style="width:70%"><tr><td style="text-align:center;border:none">__________________________<br>Rodrigo Carballo - Cristian Navas - Jefferson Arce - Anderson Ávila<br>Student / Estudiante</td><td style="text-align:center;border:none">__________________________<br>Ing. Javier A. García Mineros<br>Teacher / Docente</td></tr></table></body></html>